From 307ec7a9cf10b5e3a2028ccf8a1ac910e0192d9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MechCommander Redux Mac port <mac-port@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:33:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] Mac port: GPU renderer on Metal + xBR pixel-art upscale;
 app bundle launch

- MSL versions of the five shaders (src/mac/generated/shaders/*.msl.h); on
  Apple MCVulkanShaders loads them (entry main0, SDL_GPU_SHADERFORMAT_MSL) and
  MCVulkanPresenter creates the SDL GPU device on "metal".
- Pixel-art upscale (MCPixelArtUpscale, on by default on Apple,
  MCREDUX_UPSCALE=0 turns it off): the world surface keeps its 1x size and
  the composite enlarges it with an xBR-lv2 filter instead of nearest.
- Main: MCREDUX_DATA / MCREDUX_USER environment variables (an app bundle's
  LSEnvironment) when --data / --user aren't given.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
